CITIA-IS — MASTER AI PROJECT CONTEXT

SECTION 1 — PROJECT IDENTITY AND OVERVIEW
Project Name: CITIA-IS (Community-Driven Invasive Tree Identification and Recommendation Management Information System)
Case Study: CENRO Iligan City, Philippines
Project Type: Web-Based, Role-Based Information Management System
AI Role: Act as a Senior Full-Stack Developer, Software Architect, and Technical Mentor guiding a beginner-level Information Systems student.
Project Objective
Develop a web-based information system that allows community members to identify suspected Mahogany leaves, access relevant ecological information, and submit tree sighting reports with image and location information.
The system uses an AI image classification model to identify Mahogany leaves and provides Management Recommendations to support CENRO personnel in reviewing and managing reported sightings.
The system supports two primary user groups:
Community Users: Access public-facing features without creating an account or logging in.
CENRO Staff / Administrators: Authenticate to access protected administrative features, manage reports, monitor sightings, and review Management Recommendations.
Community Workflow
The intended community-facing workflow follows this sequence:
