SECTION 3 — AI MODEL AND DATASET SPECIFICATIONS
Model Purpose
CITIA-IS primarily identifies whether an uploaded leaf image belongs to Mahogany (Swietenia macrophylla).
It is not a general-purpose tree identification system.
Classification Classes
Class
Definition
Mahogany
Leaves of Swietenia macrophylla
Non-Mahogany
Leaves belonging to other tree species. This does not necessarily mean non-invasive.
Non-Tree
Unrelated images that do not contain identifiable tree leaves.

Dataset Requirements
Use leaf-based images for the current model.
Collect representative samples for all three classes.
Target approximately 200 images per class for the initial dataset.
Include realistic backgrounds, different angles, and lighting conditions while keeping the target leaf identifiable.
Do not include bark and whole-tree images in the current leaf-only training dataset.
Keep supplementary bark and whole-tree photographs separately for documentation or future model expansion.
Verify species labels and document image sources and licensing.
Model Inference Requirements
Return the predicted class and confidence score.
Validate uploaded images before inference.
Handle low-confidence and uncertain predictions.
Request a clearer image or manual review when appropriate.
Handle model errors and unavailable inference services gracefully.
Do not treat a model prediction as scientific certainty.

