SECTION 8 — SECURITY AND DATA INTEGRITY
Security must be considered throughout the application.
Authentication and Authorization
Protect administrative routes and endpoints.
Enforce role-based access control.
Never trust client-provided user roles or permissions.
Validate staff authorization independently on protected backend operations.
Credentials and Secrets
Never expose database passwords, Supabase service-role keys, private API credentials, or authentication secrets in frontend code.
Use appropriate environment variables and secure server-side configuration.
Never include real credentials in source code, logs, documentation, or examples.
Image Upload Security
Validate actual file content, not only file extensions.
Restrict allowed file types and upload sizes.
Handle invalid and potentially malicious files.
Use secure storage permissions.
Prevent unauthorized access to private uploaded images.
Data Integrity
Preserve submitted sighting records and classification results.
Maintain appropriate audit records for administrative review decisions.
Validate database relationships and constraints.
Handle duplicate submissions and failed transactions appropriately.

